  "description_short": "National Parks camp offering stunning coastal trails, ocean-view chalets, and a restaurant with hearty South African fare.",
  "description_long": "Nestled within the Garden Route National Park, Storms River Mouth Restcamp delivers an authentic wilderness experience where the Storms River meets the Indian Ocean. The camp's restaurant serves wholesome, unfussy meals — think robust breakfasts, line-fish specials, and traditional potjiekos — perfect for refuelling after hiking the suspension bridge or exploring the coastal trails.\n\nThe setting is remarkable: dramatic cliffs, indigenous forest, and that iconic bridge swaying above the river gorge. Accommodation ranges from self-catering chalets to oceanfront units, but even day visitors come for the scenery and a decent meal. It's family-friendly, unpretentious, and utterly restorative.\n\nThis isn't fine dining — it's honest park fare served with million-rand views. Book ahead during peak season, bring layers for the coastal wind, and leave the city behind.",
